### 9\. List and delete Docker images (Step 7 in your manual)

First, list all Docker images:

```bash
docker images
```

You should find:

```text
program5-jenkins    latest
```

Delete the image:

```bash
docker image rm program5-jenkins:latest
```

Important: If the container is still using this image, Docker will not allow you to remove it. First stop and remove the container:

```bash
docker compose down
```

Then:

```bash
docker image rm program5-jenkins:latest
```

This completes the cleanup.

Note: `docker compose down` preserves the named `jenkins_home` volume by default, so your Jenkins data remains available.

